  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">R&#xe9;ponse rapide d&apos;&apos;urgence en mati&#xe8;re de Nutrition et de protection pour les enfants et les femmes les plus vuln&#xe9;rables dans les r&#xe9;gions de Gao, M&#xe9;naka, Mopti, S&#xe9;gou au Mali</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of this project is to provide life-saving nutrition, child protection and education assistance to IDPs and host communities in Gao, Mopti and Segou regions. This UNICEF project conducts active malnutrition screening; provides integrated management of children suffering from severe acute malnutrition; delivers psycho-social support by establishing child-friendly safe spaces; providing emergency care for unaccompanied children, former child soldiers and victims of sexual- and gender-based violence; and improves access to equitable education by training teachers and distributing education kits. The project provides life-saving nutrition assistance to 165,000 people, including 65,000 women and 100,000 children ; life-saving child protection assistance to 7,574 people, including 182 women and 7,210 children; life-saving education assistance to 2,000 children.</narrative>
  </description>
